{
  "1 call site/A source location where a function is called, not a website.": "1 ƈȧȧŀŀ şīŧḗḗ",
  "{0} call sites/Source locations where a function is called, not websites.": "{0} ƈȧȧŀŀ şīŧḗḗş",
  "1 function/Counts the functions a body was copied into by inlining.": "1 ƒŭŭƞƈŧīǿǿƞ",
  "{0} functions/Counts the functions a body was copied into by inlining.": "{0} ƒŭŭƞƈŧīǿǿƞş",
  "1 instr/Abbreviation of \"machine instruction\".Keep the abbreviation short - it sits in a one-line CodeLens.": "1 īƞşŧř",
  "{0} instr/Abbreviation of \"machine instructions\".Keep the abbreviation short - it sits in a one-line CodeLens.": "{0} īƞşŧř",
  "1 spill/Register allocation term: a value the compiler had to write out to the stack because no CPU register was free.Use the established term in your language, not \"spill\" as in a spilled liquid.": "1 şƥīŀŀ",
  "{0} spills/Register allocation term: values the compiler had to write out to the stack because no CPU register was free.Use the established term in your language, not \"spill\" as in a spilled liquid.": "{0} şƥīŀŀş",
  "1 reload/Register allocation term: reading a spilled value back from the stack into a CPU register.The counterpart of \"spill\".": "1 řḗḗŀǿǿȧȧḓ",
  "{0} reloads/Register allocation term: reading spilled values back from the stack into CPU registers.The counterpart of \"spill\".": "{0} řḗḗŀǿǿȧȧḓş",
  "Instructions/Machine/IR instructions in the called function that the optimizer could not fold away.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Īƞşŧřŭŭƈŧīǿǿƞş",
  "Calls inside callee/Cost charged for the calls the called function itself makes.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Ƈȧȧŀŀş īƞşīḓḗḗ ƈȧȧŀŀḗḗḗḗ",
  "Switch lowering/Cost of turning a switch statement into jump tables and comparison chains.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Şẇīŧƈħ ŀǿǿẇḗḗřīƞɠ",
  "Argument setup/Cost of preparing the arguments passed to a call.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "ȦȦřɠŭŭḿḗḗƞŧ şḗḗŧŭŭƥ",
  "Indirect calls/Cost charged for calls through a function pointer, whose target is not known.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Īƞḓīřḗḗƈŧ ƈȧȧŀŀş",
  "Cold calling convention/Cost charged because the called function uses the calling convention for rarely executed code.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Ƈǿǿŀḓ ƈȧȧŀŀīƞɠ ƈǿǿƞṽḗḗƞŧīǿǿƞ",
  "Relative loads/Cost of loads made through a relative offset, as used by virtual call tables.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Řḗḗŀȧȧŧīṽḗḗ ŀǿǿȧȧḓş",
  "Stack promotion savings/A saving, shown as a negative number: inlining would let the optimizer keep a stack variable in registers.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Şŧȧȧƈķ ƥřǿǿḿǿǿŧīǿǿƞ şȧȧṽīƞɠş",
  "Eliminated loads/A saving, shown as a negative number: inlining would remove loads from memory.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "ḖḖŀīḿīƞȧȧŧḗḗḓ ŀǿǿȧȧḓş",
  "Call overhead removed/A saving, shown as a negative number: inlining removes the cost of performing the call itself.Appears in a comma-separated list of what made a call expensive to inline.": "Ƈȧȧŀŀ ǿǿṽḗḗřħḗḗȧȧḓ řḗḗḿǿǿṽḗḗḓ",
  "~{0} instructions/An approximate instruction count derived from an inline cost. Keep the leading ~ (about).": "~{0} īƞşŧřŭŭƈŧīǿǿƞş",
  "Includes the last-call-to-static bonus: the function is deleted after inlining./Explains a very large saving: this was the only remaining call to a function private to the file.": "Īƞƈŀŭŭḓḗḗş ŧħḗḗ ŀȧȧşŧ-ƈȧȧŀŀ-ŧǿǿ-şŧȧȧŧīƈ ƀǿǿƞŭŭş: ŧħḗḗ ƒŭŭƞƈŧīǿǿƞ īş ḓḗḗŀḗḗŧḗḗḓ ȧȧƒŧḗḗř īƞŀīƞīƞɠ.",
  "(weight {0}, threshold {1})/Follows \"inlined\" or \"not inlined - too costly\". {0} is the inline weight LLVM computed for the call (can be negative) and {1} the budget it had to stay under.Both are plain integers with no unit.": "(ẇḗḗīɠħŧ {0}, ŧħřḗḗşħǿǿŀḓ {1})",
  "{0}: {1}/One cost contributor: {0} is its label, e.g. \"Switch lowering\", {1} a plain integer.": "{0}: {1}",
  "{0}: {1} ({2})/The instruction contributor: {0} is its label, {1} a plain integer, {2} a reading such as \"~338 instructions\".": "{0}: {1} ({2})",
  "+{0} more/Ends a truncated list of cost contributors. {0} is how many were left out.": "+{0} ḿǿǿřḗḗ",
  "Missed reduction: {0} (argument address escapes)/{0} is a weight reduction the optimizer could not take because the address of an argument was used, so the value could not be kept in registers.A plain integer with no unit.": "Ḿīşşḗḗḓ řḗḗḓŭŭƈŧīǿǿƞ: {0} (ȧȧřɠŭŭḿḗḗƞŧ ȧȧḓḓřḗḗşş ḗḗşƈȧȧƥḗḗş)",
  "{0}, {1}/Joins two entries of a comma-separated list.": "{0}, {1}",
  "{0} {1}/Appends a \"+n more\" tail to a list.": "{0} {1}",
  "(weight {0}, threshold {1}): {2}./Follows \"not inlined - too costly\". {0} is the inline weight LLVM computed for the call and {1} the budget it had to stay under.{2} is an already-formatted list such as \"Instructions: 240, Argument setup: 14\".Both numbers are plain integers with no unit.": "(ẇḗḗīɠħŧ {0}, ŧħřḗḗşħǿǿŀḓ {1}): {2}.",
  "(weight {0}, threshold {1})./Follows \"not inlined - too costly\". {0} is the inline weight LLVM computed for the call and {1} the budget it had to stay under.Both are plain integers with no unit.": "(ẇḗḗīɠħŧ {0}, ŧħřḗḗşħǿǿŀḓ {1}).",
  "{0} {1}/{0} is a verdict such as \"inlined\", {1} its detail such as \"(weight 35, threshold 250)\".": "{0} {1}",
  "too costly/The optimizer judged the function too large to copy into the caller.": "ŧǿǿǿǿ ƈǿǿşŧŀẏ",
  "never - {0}/{0} is an English reason supplied by the LLVM optimizer and cannot be translated - leave the placeholder alone.": "ƞḗḗṽḗḗř - {0}",
  "never/The function can never be inlined, whatever its size.": "ƞḗḗṽḗḗř",
