  "**Inlined** at -O{0}/Heading of the hover shown on a call the optimizer inlined.Rendered as Markdown: ** ** makes text bold - keep the markers attached to the text they wrap.-O0 / -O1 / -O2 is a compiler optimization-level flag. Never translate it and never separate the O from its digit.": "**Īƞŀīƞḗḗḓ** ȧȧŧ -ǾǾ{0}",
  "**Inlined** at -O{0} {1}/Heading of the hover shown on a call the optimizer inlined. {1} is a detail such as \"(weight -35, threshold 337)\".Rendered as Markdown: ** ** makes text bold - keep the markers attached to the text they wrap.-O0 / -O1 / -O2 is a compiler optimization-level flag. Never translate it and never separate the O from its digit.": "**Īƞŀīƞḗḗḓ** ȧȧŧ -ǾǾ{0} {1}",
  "**Not inlined** at -O{0}: {1}/Heading of the hover shown on a call the optimizer rejected. {1} is the reason, e.g. \"too costly\".Rendered as Markdown: ** ** makes text bold - keep the markers attached to the text they wrap.-O0 / -O1 / -O2 is a compiler optimization-level flag. Never translate it and never separate the O from its digit.": "**Ƞǿǿŧ īƞŀīƞḗḗḓ** ȧȧŧ -ǾǾ{0}: {1}",
  "**Not inlined** at -O{0}: {1} {2}/Heading of the hover shown on a call the optimizer rejected. {1} is the reason, e.g. \"too costly\"; {2} a detail such as \"(weight 1730, threshold 225)\".Rendered as Markdown: ** ** makes text bold - keep the markers attached to the text they wrap.-O0 / -O1 / -O2 is a compiler optimization-level flag. Never translate it and never separate the O from its digit.": "**Ƞǿǿŧ īƞŀīƞḗḗḓ** ȧȧŧ -ǾǾ{0}: {1} {2}",
  "- {0}/Markdown list item - keep the leading \"- \", it is what makes the list render.": "- {0}",
  "**{0}** at -O{1}/Heading of the function-detail hover. {0} is a function name.Rendered as Markdown: ** ** makes text bold - keep the markers attached to the text they wrap.-O0 / -O1 / -O2 is a compiler optimization-level flag. Never translate it and never separate the O from its digit.": "**{0}** ȧȧŧ -ǾǾ{1}",
  "No code emitted - the optimizer inlined or removed this function./Replaces the size counters when nothing was emitted for the function.": "Ƞǿǿ ƈǿǿḓḗḗ ḗḗḿīŧŧḗḗḓ - ŧħḗḗ ǿǿƥŧīḿīẑḗḗř īƞŀīƞḗḗḓ ǿǿř řḗḗḿǿǿṽḗḗḓ ŧħīş ƒŭŭƞƈŧīǿǿƞ.",
  "- Function size: {0} bytes/Size of this function's machine code in the object file.Markdown list item - keep the leading \"- \", it is what makes the list render.": "- Ƒŭŭƞƈŧīǿǿƞ şīẑḗḗ: {0} ƀẏŧḗḗş",
  "- Machine instructions: {0}/Count of CPU instructions emitted for this function.Markdown list item - keep the leading \"- \", it is what makes the list render.": "- Ḿȧȧƈħīƞḗḗ īƞşŧřŭŭƈŧīǿǿƞş: {0}",
  "- Stack frame: {0} bytes/Stack space this function reserves for its locals and spills.Markdown list item - keep the leading \"- \", it is what makes the list render.": "- Şŧȧȧƈķ ƒřȧȧḿḗḗ: {0} ƀẏŧḗḗş",
  "- Register: {0}, {1}/Register allocator counters; {0} and {1} arrive already formatted, e.g. \"2 spills\" and \"1 reload\".Markdown list item - keep the leading \"- \", it is what makes the list render.": "- Řḗḗɠīşŧḗḗř: {0}, {1}",
  "_The individual call sites are not available for this function._/Shown when the body was inlined somewhere but the call sites cannot be listed.Rendered as Markdown: _ _ makes text italic - keep the markers attached to the text they wrap.": "_Ŧħḗḗ īƞḓīṽīḓŭŭȧȧŀ ƈȧȧŀŀ şīŧḗḗş ȧȧřḗḗ ƞǿǿŧ ȧȧṽȧȧīŀȧȧƀŀḗḗ ƒǿǿř ŧħīş ƒŭŭƞƈŧīǿǿƞ._",
  "{0} ({1})/{0} is an inline weight (plain integer), {1} a reading such as \"~338 instructions\".": "{0} ({1})",
  "- Inline weight: {0}/What the optimizer estimates copying this function into a caller costs. {0} arrives formatted, e.g. \"1730 (~338 instructions)\".Markdown list item - keep the leading \"- \", it is what makes the list render.": "- Īƞŀīƞḗḗ ẇḗḗīɠħŧ: {0}",
  "- Inline weight: {0} to {1}/A range of inline cost estimates across call sites; both arrive formatted, e.g. \"1690 (~338 instructions)\".Markdown list item - keep the leading \"- \", it is what makes the list render.": "- Īƞŀīƞḗḗ ẇḗḗīɠħŧ: {0} ŧǿǿ {1}",
  "cflat: line {0} produced no IR - showing the nearest emitted line {1}/Status bar message. IR = LLVM Intermediate Representation; keep \"IR\" as-is.{0} and {1} are source line numbers.": "ƈƒŀȧȧŧ: ŀīƞḗḗ {0} ƥřǿǿḓŭŭƈḗḗḓ ƞǿǿ ĪŘ - şħǿǿẇīƞɠ ŧħḗḗ ƞḗḗȧȧřḗḗşŧ ḗḗḿīŧŧḗḗḓ ŀīƞḗḗ {1}",
  "cflat: line {0} produced no assembly - showing the nearest emitted line {1}/Status bar message. \"assembly\" means the emitted machine-code listing.{0} and {1} are source line numbers.": "ƈƒŀȧȧŧ: ŀīƞḗḗ {0} ƥřǿǿḓŭŭƈḗḗḓ ƞǿǿ ȧȧşşḗḗḿƀŀẏ - şħǿǿẇīƞɠ ŧħḗḗ ƞḗḗȧȧřḗḗşŧ ḗḗḿīŧŧḗḗḓ ŀīƞḗḗ {1}",
  "$(watch) {0} view: cached/$(watch) is a VS Code icon token, not text. Leave it exactly as written, including the parentheses.{0} is a view label such as \"IR\" or \"asm -O2\", produced by the extension and not translated.": "$(watch) {0} ṽīḗḗẇ: ƈȧȧƈħḗḗḓ",
  "cflat view served from the response cache/Status bar tooltip: the shown output was reused, not recomputed.": "ƈƒŀȧȧŧ ṽīḗḗẇ şḗḗřṽḗḗḓ ƒřǿǿḿ ŧħḗḗ řḗḗşƥǿǿƞşḗḗ ƈȧȧƈħḗḗ",
  "$(watch) {0} view: {1}ms/$(watch) is a VS Code icon token, not text. Leave it exactly as written, including the parentheses.{0} is a view label such as \"IR\" or \"asm -O2\", produced by the extension and not translated.ms = milliseconds.": "$(watch) {0} ṽīḗḗẇ: {1}ḿş",
  "cflat view refresh: analyze {0}ms + emit {1}ms (analysis reused)/Status bar tooltip. ms = milliseconds.\"analysis reused\" means the previous parse was still valid.": "ƈƒŀȧȧŧ ṽīḗḗẇ řḗḗƒřḗḗşħ: ȧȧƞȧȧŀẏẑḗḗ {0}ḿş + ḗḗḿīŧ {1}ḿş (ȧȧƞȧȧŀẏşīş řḗḗŭŭşḗḗḓ)",
  "cflat view refresh: analyze {0}ms + emit {1}ms/Status bar tooltip. ms = milliseconds.": "ƈƒŀȧȧŧ ṽīḗḗẇ řḗḗƒřḗḗşħ: ȧȧƞȧȧŀẏẑḗḗ {0}ḿş + ḗḗḿīŧ {1}ḿş",
  "cflat: cflat.executablePath is not set. Set it in Settings to enable debugging./cflat.executablePath is a settings identifier - never translate it.\"Settings\" is the VS Code settings editor; use its localized name.": "ƈƒŀȧȧŧ: ƈƒŀȧȧŧ.ḗḗẋḗḗƈŭŭŧȧȧƀŀḗḗƤȧȧŧħ īş ƞǿǿŧ şḗḗŧ. Şḗḗŧ īŧ īƞ Şḗḗŧŧīƞɠş ŧǿǿ ḗḗƞȧȧƀŀḗḗ ḓḗḗƀŭŭɠɠīƞɠ.",
  "cflat: compiling {0}.../Progress message. {0} is a source file name.": "ƈƒŀȧȧŧ: ƈǿǿḿƥīŀīƞɠ {0}...",
  "cflat: failed to launch compiler ({0})./{0} is an operating-system error message, already in English.": "ƈƒŀȧȧŧ: ƒȧȧīŀḗḗḓ ŧǿǿ ŀȧȧŭŭƞƈħ ƈǿǿḿƥīŀḗḗř ({0}).",
  "cflat: compile failed. See \"cflat Language Server\" output for details./\"cflat Language Server\" is the name of an output panel - translate it the same way everywhere or leave it as-is.": "ƈƒŀȧȧŧ: ƈǿǿḿƥīŀḗḗ ƒȧȧīŀḗḗḓ. Şḗḗḗḗ \"ƈƒŀȧȧŧ Ŀȧȧƞɠŭŭȧȧɠḗḗ Şḗḗřṽḗḗř\" ǿǿŭŭŧƥŭŭŧ ƒǿǿř ḓḗḗŧȧȧīŀş.",
  "Show {0}/Link label in a hover. {0} arrives already formatted, e.g. \"3 call sites\".Clicking the link lists those call sites.": "Şħǿǿẇ {0}",
  "Show IR/Link label. IR = LLVM Intermediate Representation; keep \"IR\" as-is.": "Şħǿǿẇ ĪŘ",
  "Show assembly/Link label. \"assembly\" means the emitted machine-code listing.": "Şħǿǿẇ ȧȧşşḗḗḿƀŀẏ",
